<title>ITALY: ATHLETICS-LEADING MEDITERRANEAN GAMES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-LEADING MEDITERRANEAN GAMES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BARI, Italy 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in athletics</p>
<p>finals at the Mediterranean Games on Monday:</p>
<p>Men's 100 metres:</p>
<p> 1. Angelos Pavlakakis (Greece)    10.13 seconds</p>
<p>2. Anninos Markoullides (Cyprus)  10.23</p>
<p> 3. Stephane Cali (France)	   10.28</p>
<p>Women's 100 metres:</p>
<p> 1. Ekaterini Thanou (Greece)    11.13</p>
<p> 2. Frederique Bangue (France)   11.22</p>
<p> 3. Sylvanie Felix (France)	11.27</p>
<p>Men's 5,000 metres:</p>
<p> 1. Alberto Garcia (Spain)    13 minutes 25.29 seconds</p>
<p>2. Hassan Lahssini (Morocco) 13:28.95</p>
<p> 3. Said Berioui (Morocco)    13:53.98</p>
<p>Women's 5,000 metres:</p>
<p> 1. Roberta Brunet (Italy)    15:00.69</p>
<p> 2. Julia Vaquero (Spain)     15:04.48</p>
<p> 3. Zahra Ouaziz (Morocco)    15:30.19</p>
<p>Men's 3,000 metres steeplechase:</p>
<p> 1. Brahim Boulami (Morocco)   8:18.30</p>
<p>2. Hicham Bouaouich (Morocco) 8:20.30</p>
<p> 3. Giuseppe Maffei (Italy)    8:23.43</p>
<p>Men's triple jump:</p>
<p> 1. Paolo Camossi (Italy)	  16.63 metres</p>
<p>2. Christos Meletoglou (Greece) 16.50</p>
<p> 3. Germain Martial (France)     16.18</p>
<p>Women's discus:</p>
<p>1. Anastasia Kelessidou (Greece) 66.18 metres</p>
<p> 2. Styliani Tsikouna (Greece)    61.96</p>
<p> 3. Isabelle Devaluez (France)    61.28</p>
<p>Men's shot put:</p>
<p> 1. Alessandro Andrei (Italy)    19.54 metres</p>
<p> 2. Corrado Fantini (Italy)	19.19</p>
<p>3. Stevimir Ercegovac (Croatia) 19.00</p>
